{
  "slug": "tidely",
  "name": "Tidely",
  "aliases": [
    "Tidely cash flow",
    "Tidely Liquiditätsplanung"
  ],
  "description": "Tidely cash flow planning: the cash flow and forecast per month, week or day, scenarios, categories, bank accounts with balances and transactions, sales and purchase invoices, and planned values. Reads plus creating and updating invoices, plans, categories and transactions; deletes are installed switched off.",
  "instructions": "## Tidely\nThis connector uses the **Tidely Public API v2** (`https://api.tidely.com/public/v2`) of Tidely, the cash flow planning and liquidity management platform: the cash flow by period, scenarios, categories, bank accounts with balances and transactions, sales and purchase invoices, and planned values.\n\n**Setup**\n1. API access must be enabled for your Tidely account (ask Tidely support if the settings page is missing).\n2. In Tidely open **Settings, API Keys** (app.tidely.com/settings/openapi), create a key with the scopes you need (read, and write for invoices, plans, categories or transactions) and copy it into `TIDELY_API_KEY`. It is sent as the `X-Authorization` header, without a prefix.\n3. Run `tidely_verify_auth` to check the key.\n\n**Where to start**: `tidely_get_cashflow` answers most liquidity questions (balance now and forecast per month, week or day; `period` MONTH, `from` the first of a month, `to` the last day of a month). `tidely_list_scenarios` gives scenario ids, `tidely_list_categories` the category tree (parentId), `tidely_list_bank_accounts` the accounts.\n\n**Workflows**\n- Liquidity and forecast: `tidely_get_cashflow`, `tidely_list_scenarios`, `tidely_get_scenario`, `tidely_list_categories`, `tidely_get_category`.\n- Banking: `tidely_list_bank_accounts`, `tidely_get_bank_account`, `tidely_list_bank_account_balances`, `tidely_list_bank_account_transactions` (needs bankAccountId), `tidely_get_bank_account_transaction`; recategorise with `tidely_update_bank_account_transaction`. For accounts fed by an integration: `tidely_check_transactions_exist`, then `tidely_create_bank_account_transaction`.\n- Invoices: `tidely_list_invoices` and `tidely_get_invoice` (both need invoiceTypeFilter SALE or PURCHASE), `tidely_create_invoice`, `tidely_update_invoice` (e.g. mark PAID with paidDate). Invoices synced from an ERP integration are read-only.\n- Planning: `tidely_create_plan` adds a planned amount to a category and scenario; `tidely_create_category` and `tidely_update_category` manage categories.\n- Switched off at install (irreversible): `tidely_delete_invoice`, `tidely_delete_category`, `tidely_delete_plans` (all plans of a category in a scenario), `tidely_delete_bank_account_transaction`. Show the user what will be deleted and wait for a yes.\n- Also: `tidely_list_companies`, `tidely_get_company`.\n\n**Amounts and dates**: amounts are decimals in the account or company currency, negative for outgoing money and expenses. Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n**Pagination**: paged lists take `page` (from 0) and `pageSize` (default 50) and answer with `number`, `size`, `totalElements` and `totalPages`; request pages until `totalPages - 1`.\n\n**Errors** carry `error` (a stable code such as INVALID_REQUEST, INVALID_CREDENTIALS, INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE, CATEGORY_NOT_FOUND) and `message`: 400 invalid input, 401 a missing or wrong key, 403 a key without the scope for that call, 404 an unknown id. Retry 500 after a short wait; do not retry the others unchanged.\n\n**Limitations**: no money is moved; transactions and invoices are records for planning. Bulk imports, bank account creation, update and conversion, and the Partner API (OAuth, for white-label partners) are not exposed here.",
  "region": "be",
  "category": "finance",
  "icon": "tidely",
  "docsUrl": "https://developers.tidely.com/docs/overview",
  "prerequisites": "A Tidely account with API access enabled and an API key from Settings, API Keys.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "TIDELY_API_KEY"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "TIDELY_API_KEY": {
      "label": "API key",
      "kind": "credential",
      "secret": true,
      "help": "In Tidely: Settings, API Keys (app.tidely.com/settings/openapi). Create a key with the scopes you need and paste it without any prefix.",
      "link": "https://developers.tidely.com/docs/end-user/intro",
      "pattern": "^(?![Bb]earer )\\S{16,}$",
      "patternMessage": "Paste only the API key, without Bearer."
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Tidely refused the API key. Create a new one under Settings, API Keys and paste it without a prefix.",
    "403": "The key is valid but lacks the scope for this call. Edit the key's scopes under Settings, API Keys."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "tidely_verify_auth"
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Tidely Public API v2",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.tidely.com/public/v2",
    "authType": "API_KEY",
    "authConfig": {
      "headerName": "X-Authorization",
      "apiKey": "{{TIDELY_API_KEY}}"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json"
    }
  },
  "tools": [
    {
